---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Code } from "astro:components";

title: "Contributing";
description: "How to contribute to the Umi‑Time project.";
---

<Base title="Contributing">
  <div class="umi-region umi-pad">
    <main class="page page-contributing">
      <header class="page-header">
        <h1>Contributing</h1>
        <p>
          Umi‑Time is an open project. Contributions are welcome across the core
          TypeScript library, the website, and the solar‑geometry code. This page
          explains how to get started.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Repo Structure -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Repository Structure</h2>
        <p>The project uses a small monorepo layout:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>/packages/umi-time-js</strong> — the core TypeScript library
            implementing Umi‑Time, solar geometry, formatting, and parsing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>/www</strong> — the Astro-powered documentation site and demos.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>/.github</strong> — CI workflows and project automation.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Only the compiled <code>dist/</code> output from
          <code>umi-time-js</code> is published to npm. All development happens in
          <code>src/</code>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Getting Started -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Getting Started</h2>

        <p>Clone the repository and install dependencies:</p>

        <Code
          code={`git clone https://github.com/umi-time/umi-time.git
cd umi-time
npm install`}
          lang="bash"
          theme="dracula"
        />

        <p><strong>Note:</strong> All workspace commands must be run from the repository root.</p>

        <p>Build the core library:</p>

        <Code
          code={`npm run build --workspace=packages/umi-time-js`}
          lang="bash"
          theme="dracula"
        />

        <p>Start the documentation site:</p>

        <Code
          code={`npm run dev --workspace=www`}
          lang="bash"
          theme="dracula"
        />
      </section>

      <!-- Making Changes -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Making Changes</h2>
        <p>Before opening a pull request:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Ensure TypeScript builds cleanly</li>
          <li>Run the test suite</li>
          <li>Follow existing code style and naming conventions</li>
          <li>Update documentation if your change affects the public API</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Run tests:</p>

        <Code
          code={`npm test --workspace=packages/umi-time-js`}
          lang="bash"
          theme="dracula"
        />
      </section>

      <!-- Coding Standards -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Coding Standards</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Use TypeScript for all core library code</li>
          <li>Prefer pure functions for solar calculations</li>
          <li>Keep <code>UmiTime</code> immutable — methods return new instances</li>
          <li>Document public methods with clear intent and units</li>
          <li>Write tests for new solar geometry functions</li>
          <li>Keep formatting spec constants synchronized with the Umi‑Time standard</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Website Contributions -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Website Contributions</h2>
        <p>
          The documentation site lives in <code>/www</code> and is built with Astro.
          Contributions include:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Improving documentation pages</li>
          <li>Fixing layout or styling issues</li>
          <li>Enhancing interactive demos (map, clock, solar visualizations)</li>
          <li>Adding new examples or tutorials</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Start the site locally:</p>

        <Code
          code={`npm run dev --workspace=www`}
          lang="bash"
          theme="dracula"
        />
      </section>

      <!-- Pull Requests -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Pull Requests</h2>
        <p>Every pull request should:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Build successfully</li>
          <li>Pass all tests</li>
          <li>Include updated docs if needed</li>
          <li>Reference related issues</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Keep PRs focused. Small, well-scoped changes are easier to review and merge.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Issues -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Issues & Feature Requests</h2>
        <p>If you find a bug or want to propose a feature, open an issue on GitHub.</p>

        <p>Please include:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Clear reproduction steps</li>
          <li>Expected vs actual behavior</li>
          <li>Environment details (browser, OS, Node version)</li>
          <li>Any relevant Umi‑Time input values</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Thanks -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Thank You</h2>
        <p>
          Umi‑Time is a community effort. Whether you’re fixing a typo, improving
          documentation, or contributing solar geometry code, your help is appreciated.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>
